00000.jsonl:13:{\"step_index\":12,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-19T02:49:58Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-10-18T23:49:58-03:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-10-18T23:49:58-03:00\\nFile Path: `file:///tmp/h-U0pC3d/push.sh`\\nTotal Lines: 7\\nTotal Bytes: 276\\nShowing lines 1 to 7\\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: \u003cline_number\u003e: \u003coriginal_line\u003e. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\\n1: #!/usr/bin/env bash\\n2: # usage: ./push.sh event.json   (needs INTERVALS_API_KEY and ATHLETE_ID)\\n3: set -eu\\n4: curl -sS -u \\\"API_KEY:${INTERVALS_API_KEY}\\\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\\\\n5:   -X POST \\\"https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/${ATHLETE_ID}/events\\\" \\\\\\n6:   --data-binary @\\\"$1\\\"\\n7: \\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\\n\"}\r\n/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/d3763850-e4f5-4e7e-9987-6d0de49129df/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000000.jsonl:13:{\"step_index\":12,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-19T02:49:58Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-10-18T23:49:58-03:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-10-18T23:49:58-03:00\\nFile Path: `file:///tmp/h-U0pC3d/push.sh`\\nTotal Lines: 7\\nTotal Bytes: 276\\nShowing lines 1 to 7\\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: \u003cline_number\u003e: \u003coriginal_line\u003e. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\\n1: #!/usr/bin/env bash\\n2: # usage: ./push.sh event.json   (needs INTERVALS_API_KEY and ATHLETE_ID)\\n3: set -eu\\n4: curl -sS -u \\\"API_KEY:${INTERVALS_API_KEY}\\\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\\\\n5:   -X POST \\\"https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/${ATHLETE_ID}/events\\\" \\\\\\n6:   --data-binary @\\\"$1\\\"\\n7: \\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\\n\"}\r\n/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/d3763850-e4f5-4e7e-9987-6d0de49129df/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000000.jsonl:15:{\"step_index\":14,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-19T02:50:01Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-10-18T23:50:01-03:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-10-18T23:50:01-03:00\\n\\nThe command exited with code 0.\\nOutput:\\ncommit a7c6ffdb5e1c6649a4b6b0a8f83186d5a2e96f13 (HEAD -\u003e main)\\r\\nAuthor: dev \u003cdev@local\u003e\\r\\nDate:   Sun Oct 18 23:49:40 2026 -0300\\r\\n\\r\\n    base\\r\\n\\r\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\r\\nnew file mode 100644\\r\\nindex 0000000..31b0941\\r\\n--- /dev/null\\r\\n+++ b/README.md\\r\\n@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@\\r\\n+# tri-planner\\r\\n+\\r\\n+Generates structured triathlon workouts and pushes them to Intervals.icu, which\\r\\n+exports them to the athlete's Garmin watch through Garmin Connect.\\r\\n+\\r\\n+- `gen.py` turns a plan (`plans/*.json`) into the body for\\r\\n+  `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` (an event with `workout_doc`).\\r\\n+- `push.sh` posts it (needs `INTERVALS_API_KEY` and `ATHLETE_ID`).\\r\\n+- `readback/` holds what the API returned for the last pushed event and\\r\\n+  notes on what the watch displayed.\\r\\n+\\r\\n+Athlete thresholds live in Intervals (LTHR 172 for this athlete). HR targets\\r\\n+in plans are percentages of LTHR; Intervals converts them to bpm at export.\\r\\n+\\r\\n+```\\r\\n+python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json \u003e event.json\\r\\n+./push.sh event.json\\r\\n+```\\r\\ndiff --git a/gen.py b/gen.py\\r\\nnew file mode 100755\\r\\nindex 0000000..be0b3bc\\r\\n--- /dev/null\\r\\n+++ b/gen.py\\r\\n@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@\\r\\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\\r\\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Bui\n\u003ctruncated 72425 of 82303 bytes from the middle of the output\u003e\nerated/logs/transcript.jsonl:28:{\"step_index\":27,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-19T02:30:47Z\",\"input_tokens\":2754,\"cache_read_tokens\":25138,\"output_tokens\":64,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"search_web\",\"args\":{\"query\":\"\\\"site:forum.intervals.icu \\\\\\\"workout_doc\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\" garmin export\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Searching Intervals forum for workout_doc description garmin export\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search workout_doc description garmin export\\\"\"}}]}\r\n/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/f84cad17-d8bf-47b9-8a3d-f31dfb5a53c3/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl:29:{\"step_index\":28,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-19T02:30:50Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-10-18T23:30:50-03:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-10-18T23:30:54-03:00\\nThe search for \\\"site:forum.intervals.icu \\\"workout_doc\\\" \\\"description\\\" garmin export\\\" returned the following summary:\\nBased on discussions on the Intervals.icu forum regarding API usage, workout descriptions, and Garmin exports, here is how `workout_doc`, workout descriptions, and Garmin exports interact:\\n\\n### 1. How `workout_doc` is Generated\\n* **The Parser Constraint:** When you create or update a workout via the Intervals.icu API using plain text in the `description` field (using Intervals' native structured workout syntax like `- 10m 60%`), the server parses that text and populates the **`workout_doc`** object (which contains structured fields like `steps`, `duration`, `power`, etc.)[1][2]. \\n* **Client vs. Server Parsing:** Historically, the workout parser was heavily client-side, meaning text entered via the app UI immediately built out `workout_doc`[1]. However, the backend API can automatically parse native text workout syntax provided in the `description` field upon creation/update[2]. \\n\\n### 2. Exporting to Garmin Connect\\n* **The Trigger for Device Sync:** Garmin Connect integration relies on Intervals.icu processing the planned workout into a structured format that can be converted into FIT/ZWO file structures. \\n* When you enable the Garmin Connect sync option in Intervals.icu settings (allowing planned workouts to push to Garmin), Intervals pushes the structured workout data to Garmin Connect[3]. \\n* **The Role of `workout_doc`:** Garmin expects structured steps rather than raw text. The `workout_doc` structure (derived from either the Workout Builder UI or parsed text from the `description` field) is what gets translated into the device-readable structured workout format during the sync[1].\\n\\n### 3. Common Pitfalls Discussed in the Forum\\n* **Empty FIT/Sync Issues:** If workouts are created via the API improperly (e.g., bypassing text description syntax or sending malformed JSON without letting the engine parse it into `workout_do\\n\u003ctruncated 86 bytes\u003e\\nc) may turn out empty or fail to render structured steps on a Garmin device[4][2].\\n* **Syntax Matters:** When writing structured lines in the `description` field to generate a valid `workout_doc` for export, order matters. Putting distance *before* target types (e.g., putting distance before pace/HR targets) can confuse the parsing algorithm and result in Garmin receiving unstructured or improperly rendered steps[5].\\n\\nSources:\\n[1] [intervals.icu](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHfJitBNPkDphouLsHJ-jzYGWQC-hGOMMcjp96_TXVJTCMk-E8Mfzq1JxgOPrTr97zEodw1YXznh1piJjbHPVQclcxZvzhHrHbIGq2s3UEtZvklc-DBam-b6rOYEWYcgRSbiYNe7-YYjwGwDOpbVcWX5ixC)\\n[2] [intervals.icu](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHffPHgiNEQYw9I0IuZhcP6J3R_Zra3NAYMQhyYmr1XnRSCuKArN_YdIrDZJe3L8j6ziVIn0mfekhezPWUQWYwi3vtiOL9ICOuNYqytkc0ESp-NQsk6eUpHUNLtDo98WEtng52FjcI7oMnaC88qDKv6wIWLyxFe8vABNLvmqwcsk-GrlvOmxdFtixQmJ0f3X-42-llLA_Is000OkuA1